   "daf": "23a",
   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "כֵּלִים הַנִּגְמָרִים בְּטָהֳרָה כּוּ׳. דְּגַמְרִינְהוּ מַאן? אִילֵימָא דְּגַמְרִינְהוּ חָבֵר, לְמָה לְהוּ טְבִילָה?",
   "en": "§ The mishna states: «Vessels that were» fashioned and «completed in purity» require immersion for sacrificial food but not for teruma. The Gemara asks: «Who completed» the work of these vessels? «If we say that» it was «a ḥaver,» an individual who is meticulous about the halakhot of ritual purity, who «completed them, why» should «they» require «immersion,» given that he is meticulous about the halakhot of purity?"
  }
